const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"综述讨论会计与金融研究中如何把文档转换为文本度量，以及这些选择的验证困难。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The survey asks how accounting and finance research converts documents into text measures and where validation becomes difficult. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.12123",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源比较词典、语调、可读性和其他文本特征的构造与验证问题，强调文本对象和测量规则不可分离。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It compares construction and validation choices for dictionaries, tone, readability, and other text features, tying measurement to the underlying document. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.12123",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"应保存文档原件或允许访问的版本、来源与权限、首次可见时间、实体映射、特征字典和人工验证样本。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Retain source documents or permitted versions, provenance and rights, first-visible time, entity mapping, feature dictionaries, and hand-validation samples. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.12123",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"文本变量是经过选择与处理的度量，不是天然无偏的事实；公开可见也不等同于可再分发或可用于训练。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"Text variables are selected and processed measures, not naturally unbiased facts; public visibility does not imply redistribution or training rights. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.12123",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"记录抓取和版本来源，去除转载重复，区分文本发布日期与财报期，并让标签验证与模型训练保持隔离。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Record collection and version source; deduplicate reposts; distinguish publication time from reporting period; separate label validation from model training. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.12123",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Accounting Research (2016)。该综述不证明任何词典或模型在所有语言、行业和时期有效，也不授予文本或新闻的使用权。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Accounting Research (2016). The survey proves no dictionary or model works in every language, industry, or period and grants no right to use text or news. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.12123",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2016) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Textual Analysis in Accounting and Finance: A Survey”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。该综述不证明任何词典或模型在所有语言、行业和时期有效，也不授予文本或新闻的使用权。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Textual Analysis in Accounting and Finance: A Survey”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
